A||||1||contra||FieroGT vs '99 GrandPrix vs Mustang 5.0||||1||
Z||000000||contra||07-03-2000||12:02 AM||||On my way home from work today i stopped at a stop light with a riced up (yes riced up) pontiac grand prix, with all it's shiny rims and tinted windows with neon everywhere and superbass and whaletale spoiler and of course a ricecooker exhaust. But beside that there was a nicely setup mustang 5.0. As soon as the light turned green, we all goosed our cars up the small hill then down the straightaway for 2 intersections. Me in my '87 fiero Gt jumped into lead ahead of both other cars, but the grand prix was closing in on me. I was still in 2nd gear (i have an automatic and i had it in D2) As soon as the grandprix was nose to nose, i jumped my tranny into Drive and shot off ahead of the guy pretty quickly. The mustang came up like a bat out of hell tho behind us and swooped down and matched myspeed when we had to slow down because of cars turning left at the next intersection. It was quite a rush though. I can't wait until the crack in my exhaust manifold is fixed so i can get a little more horsepower. Only mods i have on the engine are an accel supercoil, K&N filter, no cat. converter, no muffler, and no EGR  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (yes i know, i should be ashamed)<P>Wellp, that's my story for the night...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dan86gt3.8||07-03-2000||01:45 AM||||was the mustang spinning up a storm?  I know that the easiest way to beat them is race from the line because all they do is spin.  But if someone has some nitto's or some et streets look out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
